WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.050
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Welcome to "Get

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:03.300
Cooking in Cloud," where
we share the best recipes

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.160
to apply in your cloud kitchen.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.387
I'm Priyanka, and
we're joined by Jenny.

00:00:07.387 --> 00:00:08.470
JENNY BROWN: Hi, everyone.

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:10.110
Today we'll be
continuing our recipe

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.800
to help Dinner Winner make the
most of their implementation.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.425
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
And of course, we'll

00:00:14.425 --> 00:00:16.540
be continuing with our
gluten-free recipe,

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.440
now that we have cleaned our
workspace of the identified

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:20.040
allergens.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.540
JENNY BROWN: We've got a few
moving pieces with this recipe,

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.330
so let's quickly
review where we've been

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.440
and where we've got to go.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.849
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:35.225 --> 00:00:36.850
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
In the last episode,

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.570
we introduced the application
called Dinner Winner.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.370
They collect recipes
from users all

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.520
over the world, review them,
and award prizes for the recipes

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.770
delicious enough to
repost on their app.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.230
JENNY BROWN: The recipes aren't
supposed to, but they might

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.060
initially contain
personal information

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:54.450
of the participants, and that
information cannot make it

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:58.030
to the judging or the final
publicly-posted recipe card.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:00.480
So there's some work to do
to make sure the automated

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.330
classification puts the
right data in the right spot

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:04.319
at the right time.

00:01:04.319 --> 00:01:06.910
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Fortunately, we've got a plan.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:09.000
This will be a
four-step process.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.700
Dinner Winner will first
create Cloud Storage Buckets

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.710
to be used as part
of the quarantine

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.840
and the classification pipeline.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.060
They would need to
create a Cloud Pub/Sub

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:21.360
topic and subscription to
notify between the two Cloud

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.350
Functions.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:25.500
Then they need to create
the two Cloud Functions, one

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.650
that invokes the DLP API
when files are uploaded,

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:32.430
and the second that uses the
DLP API to inspect and classify

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:35.280
the files and move them
to the appropriate bucket.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.940
Then finally, upload some sample
files to the quarantine bucket

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:40.213
to invoke the Cloud Function.

00:01:40.213 --> 00:01:42.630
JENNY BROWN: Now let's start
by creating the Cloud Storage

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:43.140
Bucket.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:44.910
But before we can
even do that, we

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.710
need to set up our environment.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.950
Create or select the GCP
project and make sure billing

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:51.120
is enabled.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.310
Then head over to
the APIs and services

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:56.700
and enable APIs for Cloud
Functions, Cloud Storage,

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.550
and Cloud Data Loss
Prevention APIs.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.750
Now that we have
the APIs enabled,

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.360
let's enable the
correct permissions

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.280
so that our App Engine
service account can

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.740
connect with the DLP API.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:11.610
For that, we will open the IAM
&amp; admin page in our project,

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:15.220
locate the App Engine service
account, and edit the roles.

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:19.110
Add project owner, DLP
administrator, and DLP API

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.420
service agent, and save.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.670
Next, we'll grant the
DLP service account

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.470
the permission that it needs.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:29.220
Locate the DLP API service agent
and add a project viewer's role

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:29.720
to it.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.845
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Now
we're ready to get our Cloud

00:02:31.845 --> 00:02:32.970
Storage Buckets created.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:35.430
We navigate to Cloud
Storage and create them.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.650
Remember, we will need
three buckets, one

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.690
for sensitive data, one
for non-sensitive data,

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:44.070
and the last one for all
the files as they come in.

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:46.350
Name the buckets as
you wish, but remember,

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:49.690
it has to be a
globally unique name.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.510
Once we have created
all three buckets,

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:55.120
you should be able to see them
all in the storage browser.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.720
Now we are ready to set
up our Cloud Pub/Sub

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.430
topic and subscription.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:02.310
Let's navigate to Cloud
Pub/Sub and create a topic,

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.740
provide it a name,
and hit Create.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:07.500
Then to create a subscription
corresponding to the topic,

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.447
click on New Subscription,
provide it a name, and Create.

00:03:10.447 --> 00:03:12.780
JENNY BROWN: At this point,
we've got the setup in place

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.030
for Dinner Winner and we
have two more steps left.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.950
But now that we've
got our process

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.650
and our contaminant-free
environment, let's get baking.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.030
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
What a recipe.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:23.500
This gluten-free
thing is no joke,

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.610
but it's critical to have an
understanding of what goes in

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:27.598
and what stays out.

00:03:27.598 --> 00:03:29.140
JENNY BROWN: It's
a delicate balance,

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:30.453
but we're halfway there.

00:03:30.453 --> 00:03:33.120
Stay tuned for next week when we
get Dinner Winner to the finish

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.530
line for their implementation.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:37.245
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Automated
classification, here we come.

00:03:37.245 --> 00:03:40.230
For more information about
alternative approaches,

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.660
do check out the articles
linked in the description below.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.452
JENNY BROWN: And if
you're hungry for more,

00:03:44.452 --> 00:03:46.800
be sure to like, subscribe,
and catch up on all the ways

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.300
you can get cooking with Cloud.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.650
[MUSIC PLAYING]

